                <pb facs="0241" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.92/125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-11T17:00:00+02:00">December 11, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1117. Chauvel confirmed to me yesterday Laval’s statements regarding French
                    refusal of the Japanese offer to arbitrate the Indochina–Thailand conflict. He
                    thought that for the time being an effort <pb facs="0242" n="234" xml:id="pg234"
                    /> would be made to settle matters directly between Indochina and Thailand. He
                    promised to show me the telegram [to] Tokyo now in preparation as soon as it had
                    been approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
